SUMMARY:Pride Month Terrarium Workshop
DESCRIPTION:Get creative this Pride Month and join us for a fun-filled terrarium workshop!\nCalling all plant lovers! Have you ever wanted to build your own terrarium? In celebration of Pride Month\, join fellow plant-loving queers to create your own miniature ecosystem—your very own container oasis. This hands-on workshop is open to all\, no experience required.\n \nWe know Pride can be joyful\, vibrant\, and sometimes a little overwhelming. This workshop offers a space to slow down\, connect\, and create something grounding—an oasis you can return to for moments of calm and reflection. Come express yourself through terrarium-building!\n \nContainers and planting materials will be provided\, and we encourage participants to bring their own containers from home to personalize and transform.\n \nThursday\, June 11 from 6 to 8 p.m.\nPublic $65\, TBG Members $60 (plus applicable taxes and fees).\n \nAbout Bree Jiang\n \nBree Jiang (she/they) is a multidisciplinary artist and facilitator based in Toronto. Throughout her arts practice\, she is inspired by queer ecology and finding metaphors for queer and trans expression within nature. Her lifelong awe of nature has translated into a love of creating enclosed ecosystems.\n \nBree has facilitated terrarium-making workshops and spoken about the joys of creating bioactive terrariums\, including with the Garden Club of Toronto. She is one half of Venusrium (@venusrium)\, a collective founded by two trans women of colour that aims to foster community connection for BIPOC and 2SLGBTQIA+ people through terrarium-making and plant-based workshops. More of her work can be found at @_breejiang.\n \nJoin Toronto Botanical Garden\n \nJoin the Toronto Botanical Garden (TBG) as a member to get a discount on this program\, upcoming events and classes\, and free parking. A TBG membership helps you deepen your knowledge and connection to the natural world\, become a part of a dynamic community of plant people\, and be inspired! Become a member!\n \nAdditional Program Information\n\n\n\nPlease review our Refund Policy and Terms of Agreement.\nFor more information on accessibility at the garden please review our Accessibility Features webpage. If you have any accessibility requirements during your program please email programsupport@torontobotanicalgarden.ca.\nTo learn more about the Toronto Botanical Garden and our programs\, please review our list of Frequently Asked Questions.
URL:https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/event/pride-month-terrarium-workshop/
LOCATION:Toronto Botanical Garden\, 777 Lawrence Ave E\, Toronto\, ON\, M3C 1P2\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Gardening
